# Memory Bank: backend/src/routes/project.routes.ts

## Purpose
This file defines the Express router for all project-related API endpoints, including sub-resources like tasks, subtasks, and materials associated with a project. It maps HTTP request paths and methods to specific controller actions.

## How it Works
- An Express `Router` instance is created.
- Middleware like `isAuthenticated` is applied to routes requiring user authentication.
- Controller methods (e.g., `projectController.createProject`, `materialController.getMaterialsByProject`) are bound to specific route paths and HTTP methods (POST, GET, PUT, DELETE).
- The router is exported for use in the main application setup (e.g., in `server.ts` or `index.ts`).

## Key Endpoints Defined
- `/projects`:
  - `POST /`: Create a new project.
  - `GET /`: Get all projects.
- `/projects/:projectId`:
  - `GET /:projectId`: Get a project by its ID.
  - `PUT /:projectId`: Update a project.
  - `DELETE /:projectId`: Delete a project.
- `/projects/:projectId/tasks`:
  - `POST /:projectId/tasks`: Create a new task for a project.
  - `GET /:projectId/tasks`: Get all tasks for a project.
- `/projects/tasks/:taskId`: (Note: Path structure might vary slightly based on actual implementation, e.g. `/tasks/:taskId`)
  - `PUT /tasks/:taskId`: Update a task.
  - `DELETE /tasks/:taskId`: Delete a task.
  - `PUT /tasks/:taskId/status`: Update the status of a task.
- `/projects/tasks/:taskId/subtasks`: (Note: Path structure might vary slightly)
  - `POST /tasks/:taskId/subtasks`: Create a subtask for a task.
  - `GET /tasks/:taskId/subtasks`: Get all subtasks for a task.
- `/projects/subtasks/:subtaskId`: (Note: Path structure might vary slightly)
  - `PUT /subtasks/:subtaskId`: Update a subtask.
  - `DELETE /subtasks/:subtaskId`: Delete a subtask.
- **Materials (New/Updated Section)**
  - `/projects/:projectId/materials`:
    - `POST /:projectId/materials`: Create a new material for a project. (Controller: `materialController.createMaterial`)
    - `GET /:projectId/materials`: Get all materials for a project. (Controller: `materialController.getMaterialsByProject`)
  - `/projects/materials/:materialId`: (Note: Path structure might vary slightly, e.g. `/materials/:materialId`)
    - `GET /materials/:materialId`: Get a specific material by its ID. (Controller: `materialController.getMaterialById`)
    - `PUT /materials/:materialId`: Update a material. (Controller: `materialController.updateMaterial`)
    - `DELETE /materials/:materialId`: Delete a material. (Controller: `materialController.deleteMaterial`)

## Inputs
- HTTP Request objects from clients.
- Data from request bodies (for POST/PUT).
- Parameters from request paths (e.g., `projectId`, `taskId`, `materialId`).
- User authentication details (via `isAuthenticated` middleware).

## Outputs
- HTTP Response objects sent to clients, typically containing JSON data or status codes.

## Dependencies
- `express`: For router functionality.
- `../controllers/project`: For project, task, and subtask controller instances.
- `../controllers/material.controller`: For material controller instance.
- `../middlewares/auth.middleware`: For `isAuthenticated` middleware.

## Recent Changes (2025-05-10)
- Added routes for material management under `/projects/:projectId/materials` and `/materials/:materialId`.
- Imported `materialController` to handle these new routes.
- Ensured `isAuthenticated` middleware is applied to material routes.
- **TypeScript Error Resolution (TS2769)**: Type errors related to `CustomRequest` in this file were resolved. This was achieved by modifying `backend/src/controllers/project.controller.ts` to remove its local `AuthenticatedRequest` interface and instead import and use the standardized `CustomRequest` from `backend/src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts`. This ensures type consistency for request objects processed by `isAuthenticated` middleware. No direct changes were made to `project.routes.ts` itself for this fix, as the errors originated from type incompatibilities with the controller.

## Flow Diagram (Conceptual)
```mermaid
graph TD
    ClientRequest[Client HTTP Request] -->|e.g., GET /projects/123/materials| ExpressApp{Express App}
    ExpressApp --> ProjectRouter{project.routes.ts}
    ProjectRouter --matches--> RouteHandler{Specific Route Handler, e.g., router.get('/:projectId/materials', ...)}
    RouteHandler --> IsAuthenticated{isAuthenticated Middleware}
    IsAuthenticated --Authenticated--> MaterialController{materialController.getMaterialsByProject}
    MaterialController --> MaterialService{MaterialService}
    MaterialService --> MaterialRepository{MaterialRepository/DB}
    MaterialRepository --> MaterialService
    MaterialService --> MaterialController
    MaterialController -->|JSON Response| ClientResponse[Client HTTP Response]
    IsAuthenticated --Not Authenticated--> UnauthorizedResponse[401 Unauthorized]
    UnauthorizedResponse --> ClientResponse
